A. Add constants near RISK_WEIGHTS:
```rust
/// Number of recent commits whose touched files receive the recency boost.
/// Picks up the session's own edit targets: one-off fixes land in the last
/// few commits, so a short window is enough to catch the `update.rs`-shaped
/// miss that all 30-day signals systematically under-weight.
const RECENT_TOUCH_WINDOW: usize = 5;

/// Additive boost granted to files touched within the last `RECENT_TOUCH_WINDOW`
/// commits (or with uncommitted working-tree changes). Sized relative to the
/// largest single historical weight (churn = 0.30): being touched in the
/// recent past is at least as strong a predictor of the *next* edit target as
/// being the most-churned file in the repo. Without this, a one-off fix file
/// with modest churn/revert/coupling history never surfaces into the top-N.
const RECENT_TOUCH_BOOST: f64 = 0.40;
```

B. Helper to collect recently-touched files:
```rust
/// Collect `src/**/*.rs` files touched within the last `window` commits on
/// HEAD, plus any src file with uncommitted working-tree/staged changes
/// (i.e. this session's own edits). Best-effort: empty set on git errors.
fn recently_touched_src_files(window: usize) -> std::collections::HashSet<String> {
    let mut out = std::collections::HashSet::new();
    // Recent commits on HEAD
    if let Ok(output) = crate::git::run_git(&[
        "log",
        &format!("-{window}"),
        "--name-only",
        "--pretty=format:",
    ]) {
        for line in output.lines() {
            let path = line.trim();
            if is_src_rust_path(path) {
                out.insert(path.to_string());
            }
        }
    }
    // Uncommitted: staged (`--cached`) + unstaged working tree
    for args in [&["diff", "--cached", "--name-only"][..], &["diff", "--name-only"][..]] {
        if let Ok(output) = crate::git::run_git(args) {
            for line in output.lines() {
                let path = line.trim();
                if is_src_rust_path(path) {
                    out.insert(path.to_string());
                }
            }
        }
    }
    out
}
```

