```rust
/// Risk signal weights: [churn, recency, size, complexity, test_density, coupling, revert_history].
///
/// These seven weights must sum to 1.0. The revert_history weight (0.10) captures
/// empirical failure data — files that have been reverted are more likely to cause
/// future regressions. The complexity proxy (0.10) estimates cyclomatic complexity
/// via branch/match density. This is the signal set that makes the risk scorer learn
/// from its own history rather than just measuring static properties.
///
/// Churn was trimmed (0.30 → 0.25) and recency raised (0.15 → 0.20) after the
/// day-175 calibration miss: the scorer flagged 10 files as high-risk (none
/// broke) while missing `src/update.rs`, a one-off fix target that was recently
/// touched but historically quiet. Combined with the `RECENT_TOUCH_BUMP` for
/// files touched in the last `RECENT_COMMIT_WINDOW` commits (or dirty in the
/// working tree), the scorer now favors near-term edit targets over purely
/// historical fragility.
const RISK_WEIGHTS: [f64; 7] = [0.25, 0.20, 0.15, 0.10, 0.10, 0.10, 0.10];
```

Then add constants near MUTATION_WEIGHT:

```rust
/// Files touched within the last N commits (or modified in the working tree)
/// get a recency bump — the sharper "recently touched" signal added after the
/// day-175 calibration miss (a one-off `src/update.rs` fix target was missed
/// while 10 unrealted files were flagged).
pub(crate) const RECENT_COMMIT_WINDOW: usize = 5;

/// Additive score bump for files touched in the last `RECENT_COMMIT_WINDOW`
/// commits or modified in the working tree. Sized so a recent one-off fix
/// target outranks a historically fragile but dormant file on the current
/// weight scale (scores are roughly 0–1.2).
const RECENT_TOUCH_BUMP: f64 = 0.20;
```

